msgid "Argparse Tutorial"
msgstr "Tutorial Argparse"

msgid ""
"This tutorial is intended to be a gentle introduction to :mod:`argparse`, "
"the recommended command-line parsing module in the Python standard library."
msgstr ""
"Tutorial ini dimaksudkan sebagai pengantar yang ringan "
"untuk :mod:`argparse`, modul parser baris perintah yang direkomendasikan "
"dalam pustaka standar Python."

msgid ""
"The standard library includes two other libraries directly related to "
"command-line parameter processing: the lower level :mod:`optparse` module "
"(which may require more code to configure for a given application, but also "
"allows an application to request behaviors that ``argparse`` doesn't "
"support), and the very low level :mod:`getopt` (which specifically serves as "
"an equivalent to the :c:func:`!getopt` family of functions available to C "
"programmers). While neither of those modules is covered directly in this "
"guide, many of the core concepts in ``argparse`` first originated in "
"``optparse``, so some aspects of this tutorial will also be relevant to "
"``optparse`` users."
msgstr ""
"Pustaka standar memiliki dua pustaka lain yang berkaitan langsung dengan "
"pemrosesan parameter baris perintah: modul :mod:`optparse` yang berada di "
"tingkat lebih rendah (yang mungkin membutuhkan lebih banyak kode untuk "
"dikonfigurasi pada aplikasi tertentu, tetapi juga memungkinkan aplikasi "
"meminta perilaku yang tidak didukung ``argparse``), dan :mod:`getopt` yang "
"berada di tingkat yang sangat rendah (yang secara khusus berfungsi sebagai "
"padanan keluarga fungsi :c:func:`!getopt` yang tersedia bagi pemrogram C). "
"Meskipun kedua modul tersebut tidak dibahas secara langsung dalam panduan "
"ini, banyak konsep inti dalam ``argparse`` pertama kali berasal dari "
"``optparse``, sehingga beberapa aspek tutorial ini juga akan relevan bagi "
"pengguna ``optparse``."

msgid "Concepts"
msgstr "Konsep"

msgid ""
"Let's show the sort of functionality that we are going to explore in this "
"introductory tutorial by making use of the :command:`ls` command:"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita tunjukkan jenis fungsionalitas yang akan kita jelajahi dalam "
"tutorial pengantar ini dengan menggunakan perintah :command:`ls`:"

msgid ""
"$ ls\n"
"cpython  devguide  prog.py  pypy  rm-unused-function.patch\n"
"$ ls pypy\n"
"ctypes_configure  demo  dotviewer  include  lib_pypy  lib-python ...\n"
"$ ls -l\n"
"total 20\n"
"drwxr-xr-x 19 wena wena 4096 Feb 18 18:51 cpython\n"
"drwxr-xr-x  4 wena wena 4096 Feb  8 12:04 devguide\n"
"-rwxr-xr-x  1 wena wena  535 Feb 19 00:05 prog.py\n"
"drwxr-xr-x 14 wena wena 4096 Feb  7 00:59 pypy\n"
"-rw-r--r--  1 wena wena  741 Feb 18 01:01 rm-unused-function.patch\n"
"$ ls --help\n"
"Usage: ls [OPTION]... [FILE]...\n"
"List information about the FILEs (the current directory by default).\n"
"Sort entries alphabetically if none of -cftuvSUX nor --sort is specified.\n"
"..."
msgstr ""
"$ ls\n"
"cpython  devguide  prog.py  pypy  rm-unused-function.patch\n"
"$ ls pypy\n"
"ctypes_configure  demo  dotviewer  include  lib_pypy  lib-python ...\n"
"$ ls -l\n"
"total 20\n"
"drwxr-xr-x 19 wena wena 4096 Feb 18 18:51 cpython\n"
"drwxr-xr-x  4 wena wena 4096 Feb  8 12:04 devguide\n"
"-rwxr-xr-x  1 wena wena  535 Feb 19 00:05 prog.py\n"
"drwxr-xr-x 14 wena wena 4096 Feb  7 00:59 pypy\n"
"-rw-r--r--  1 wena wena  741 Feb 18 01:01 rm-unused-function.patch\n"
"$ ls --help\n"
"Usage: ls [OPTION]... [FILE]...\n"
"List information about the FILEs (the current directory by default).\n"
"Sort entries alphabetically if none of -cftuvSUX nor --sort is specified.\n"
"..."

msgid "A few concepts we can learn from the four commands:"
msgstr ""
"Beberapa konsep yang bisa kita pelajari dari keempat perintah tersebut:"

msgid ""
"The :command:`ls` command is useful when run without any options at all. It "
"defaults to displaying the contents of the current directory."
msgstr ""
"Perintah :command:`ls` berguna saat dijalankan tanpa opsi apa pun. Secara "
"default, perintah ini menampilkan isi direktori saat ini."

msgid ""
"If we want beyond what it provides by default, we tell it a bit more. In "
"this case, we want it to display a different directory, ``pypy``. What we "
"did is specify what is known as a positional argument. It's named so because "
"the program should know what to do with the value, solely based on where it "
"appears on the command line. This concept is more relevant to a command "
"like :command:`cp`, whose most basic usage is ``cp SRC DEST``. The first "
"position is *what you want copied,* and the second position is *where you "
"want it copied to*."
msgstr ""
"Jika kita menginginkan lebih dari yang disediakannya secara default, kita "
"beri tahu sedikit lebih banyak. Dalam contoh ini, kita ingin perintah ini "
"menampilkan direktori yang berbeda, ``pypy``. Yang kita lakukan adalah "
"menetapkan apa yang dikenal sebagai argumen posisional. Disebut demikian "
"karena program harus tahu apa yang harus dilakukan dengan nilainya, semata-"
"mata berdasarkan posisinya pada baris perintah. Konsep ini lebih relevan "
"untuk perintah seperti :command:`cp`, yang penggunaan paling dasarnya adalah "
"``cp SRC DEST``. Posisi pertama adalah *apa yang ingin Anda salin*, dan "
"posisi kedua adalah *ke mana Anda ingin menyalinnya*."

msgid ""
"Now, say we want to change behaviour of the program. In our example, we "
"display more info for each file instead of just showing the file names. The "
"``-l`` in that case is known as an optional argument."
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, katakanlah kita ingin mengubah perilaku program. Dalam contoh "
"kita, kita menampilkan info lebih banyak untuk setiap berkas, bukan hanya "
"menampilkan nama berkasnya. ``-l`` dalam hal ini dikenal sebagai argumen "
"opsional."

msgid ""
"That's a snippet of the help text. It's very useful in that you can come "
"across a program you have never used before, and can figure out how it works "
"simply by reading its help text."
msgstr ""
"Itu adalah cuplikan teks bantuan. Teks ini sangat berguna karena Anda bisa "
"menemukan program yang belum pernah Anda gunakan sebelumnya, dan memahami "
"cara kerjanya hanya dengan membaca teks bantuannya."

msgid "The basics"
msgstr "Dasar-dasar"

msgid "Let us start with a very simple example which does (almost) nothing::"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita mulai dengan contoh yang sangat sederhana yang (hampir) tidak "
"melakukan apa-apa::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.parse_args()"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.parse_args()"

msgid "Following is a result of running the code:"
msgstr "Berikut adalah hasil dari menjalankan kode tersebut:"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py\n"
"$ python prog.py --help\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h]\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help  show this help message and exit\n"
"$ python prog.py --verbose\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h]\n"
"prog.py: error: unrecognized arguments: --verbose\n"
"$ python prog.py foo\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h]\n"
"prog.py: error: unrecognized arguments: foo"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py\n"
"$ python prog.py --help\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h]\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help  show this help message and exit\n"
"$ python prog.py --verbose\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h]\n"
"prog.py: error: unrecognized arguments: --verbose\n"
"$ python prog.py foo\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h]\n"
"prog.py: error: unrecognized arguments: foo"

msgid "Here is what is happening:"
msgstr "Inilah yang sedang terjadi:"

msgid ""
"Running the script without any options results in nothing displayed to "
"stdout. Not so useful."
msgstr ""
"Menjalankan skrip tanpa opsi apa pun tidak menampilkan apa pun ke stdout. "
"Tidak begitu berguna."

msgid ""
"The second one starts to display the usefulness of the :mod:`argparse` "
"module. We have done almost nothing, but already we get a nice help message."
msgstr ""
"Yang kedua mulai menunjukkan kegunaan modul :mod:`argparse`. Kita hampir "
"tidak melakukan apa-apa, tetapi kita sudah mendapatkan pesan bantuan yang "
"bagus."

msgid ""
"The ``--help`` option, which can also be shortened to ``-h``, is the only "
"option we get for free (i.e. no need to specify it). Specifying anything "
"else results in an error. But even then, we do get a useful usage message, "
"also for free."
msgstr ""
"Opsi ``--help``, yang juga dapat disingkat menjadi ``-h``, adalah satu-"
"satunya opsi yang kita dapatkan secara gratis (artinya, tidak perlu "
"menentukannya). Menentukan hal lain akan menghasilkan galat. Tetapi meskipun "
"begitu, kita tetap mendapatkan pesan penggunaan yang berguna, juga secara "
"gratis."

msgid "Introducing Positional arguments"
msgstr "Memperkenalkan argumen posisional"

msgid "An example::"
msgstr "Sebuah contoh::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"echo\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"print(args.echo)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"echo\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"print(args.echo)"

msgid "And running the code:"
msgstr "Dan menjalankan kodenya:"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] echo\n"
"prog.py: error: the following arguments are required: echo\n"
"$ python prog.py --help\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] echo\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  echo\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help  show this help message and exit\n"
"$ python prog.py foo\n"
"foo"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] echo\n"
"prog.py: error: the following arguments are required: echo\n"
"$ python prog.py --help\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] echo\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  echo\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help  show this help message and exit\n"
"$ python prog.py foo\n"
"foo"

msgid "Here is what's happening:"
msgstr "Inilah yang terjadi:"

msgid ""
"We've added the :meth:`~ArgumentParser.add_argument` method, which is what "
"we use to specify which command-line options the program is willing to "
"accept. In this case, I've named it ``echo`` so that it's in line with its "
"function."
msgstr ""
"Kita telah menambahkan metode :meth:`~ArgumentParser.add_argument`, yang "
"kita gunakan untuk menentukan opsi baris perintah apa saja yang bersedia "
"diterima program. Dalam hal ini, saya menamainya ``echo`` agar sesuai dengan "
"fungsinya."

msgid "Calling our program now requires us to specify an option."
msgstr ""
"Memanggil program kita sekarang mengharuskan kita menentukan sebuah opsi."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`~ArgumentParser.parse_args` method actually returns some data "
"from the options specified, in this case, ``echo``."
msgstr ""
"Metode :meth:`~ArgumentParser.parse_args` sebenarnya mengembalikan beberapa "
"data dari opsi yang ditentukan, dalam hal ini, ``echo``."

msgid ""
"The variable is some form of 'magic' that :mod:`argparse` performs for free "
"(i.e. no need to specify which variable that value is stored in). You will "
"also notice that its name matches the string argument given to the method, "
"``echo``."
msgstr ""
"Variabel tersebut adalah semacam 'keajaiban' yang dilakukan :mod:`argparse` "
"secara gratis (artinya, tidak perlu menentukan di variabel mana nilai "
"tersebut disimpan). Anda juga akan melihat bahwa namanya cocok dengan "
"argumen string yang diberikan ke metode tersebut, ``echo``."

msgid ""
"Note however that, although the help display looks nice and all, it "
"currently is not as helpful as it can be. For example we see that we got "
"``echo`` as a positional argument, but we don't know what it does, other "
"than by guessing or by reading the source code. So, let's make it a bit more "
"useful::"
msgstr ""
"Namun perlu diperhatikan bahwa, meskipun tampilan bantuan terlihat bagus, "
"saat ini tampilannya belum seberguna yang seharusnya. Misalnya, kita melihat "
"bahwa kita mendapatkan ``echo`` sebagai argumen posisional, tetapi kita "
"tidak tahu apa fungsinya, selain dengan menebak atau membaca kode sumber. "
"Jadi, mari kita buat sedikit lebih berguna::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"echo\", help=\"echo the string you use here\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"print(args.echo)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"echo\", help=\"echo the string you use here\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"print(args.echo)"

msgid "And we get:"
msgstr "Dan kita mendapatkan:"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py -h\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] echo\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  echo        echo the string you use here\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help  show this help message and exit"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py -h\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] echo\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  echo        echo the string you use here\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help  show this help message and exit"

msgid "Now, how about doing something even more useful::"
msgstr "Sekarang, bagaimana kalau melakukan sesuatu yang lebih berguna::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", help=\"display a square of a given "
"number\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"print(args.square**2)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", help=\"display a square of a given "
"number\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"print(args.square**2)"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"  File \"prog.py\", line 5, in <module>\n"
"    print(args.square**2)\n"
"TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for ** or pow(): 'str' and 'int'"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"  File \"prog.py\", line 5, in <module>\n"
"    print(args.square**2)\n"
"TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for ** or pow(): 'str' and 'int'"

msgid ""
"That didn't go so well. That's because :mod:`argparse` treats the options we "
"give it as strings, unless we tell it otherwise. So, let's "
"tell :mod:`argparse` to treat that input as an integer::"
msgstr ""
"Itu tidak berjalan dengan baik. Itu karena :mod:`argparse` memperlakukan "
"opsi yang kita berikan sebagai string, kecuali kita memberi tahu sebaliknya. "
"Jadi, mari kita beri tahu :mod:`argparse` untuk memperlakukan input tersebut "
"sebagai bilangan bulat::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", help=\"display a square of a given "
"number\",\n"
"                    type=int)\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"print(args.square**2)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", help=\"display a square of a given "
"number\",\n"
"                    type=int)\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"print(args.square**2)"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"16\n"
"$ python prog.py four\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] square\n"
"prog.py: error: argument square: invalid int value: 'four'"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"16\n"
"$ python prog.py four\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] square\n"
"prog.py: error: argument square: invalid int value: 'four'"

msgid ""
"That went well. The program now even helpfully quits on bad illegal input "
"before proceeding."
msgstr ""
"Itu berjalan dengan baik. Program sekarang bahkan langsung keluar ketika "
"menerima input ilegal sebelum melanjutkan."

msgid "Introducing Optional arguments"
msgstr "Memperkenalkan argumen opsional"

msgid ""
"So far we have been playing with positional arguments. Let us have a look on "
"how to add optional ones::"
msgstr ""
"Sejauh ini kita telah bermain-main dengan argumen posisional. Mari kita "
"lihat cara menambahkan argumen opsional::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"--verbosity\", help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"if args.verbosity:\n"
"    print(\"verbosity turned on\")"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"--verbosity\", help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"if args.verbosity:\n"
"    print(\"verbosity turned on\")"

msgid "And the output:"
msgstr "Dan keluarannya:"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py --verbosity 1\n"
"verbosity turned on\n"
"$ python prog.py\n"
"$ python prog.py --help\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [--verbosity VERBOSITY]\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n"
"  --verbosity VERBOSITY\n"
"                        increase output verbosity\n"
"$ python prog.py --verbosity\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [--verbosity VERBOSITY]\n"
"prog.py: error: argument --verbosity: expected one argument"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py --verbosity 1\n"
"verbosity turned on\n"
"$ python prog.py\n"
"$ python prog.py --help\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [--verbosity VERBOSITY]\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n"
"  --verbosity VERBOSITY\n"
"                        increase output verbosity\n"
"$ python prog.py --verbosity\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [--verbosity VERBOSITY]\n"
"prog.py: error: argument --verbosity: expected one argument"

msgid ""
"The program is written so as to display something when ``--verbosity`` is "
"specified and display nothing when not."
msgstr ""
"Program ditulis sedemikian rupa sehingga menampilkan sesuatu saat "
"``--verbosity`` ditentukan dan tidak menampilkan apa pun saat tidak "
"ditentukan."

msgid ""
"To show that the option is actually optional, there is no error when running "
"the program without it. Note that by default, if an optional argument isn't "
"used, the relevant variable, in this case ``args.verbosity``, is given "
"``None`` as a value, which is the reason it fails the truth test of "
"the :keyword:`if` statement."
msgstr ""
"Untuk menunjukkan bahwa opsi tersebut memang opsional, tidak ada galat saat "
"menjalankan program tanpa opsi tersebut. Perlu diperhatikan bahwa secara "
"default, jika argumen opsional tidak digunakan, variabel yang relevan, dalam "
"hal ini ``args.verbosity``, diberi nilai ``None``, yang menjadi alasan "
"mengapa variabel tersebut gagal dalam pengujian kebenaran (truth test) pada "
"pernyataan :keyword:`if`."

msgid "The help message is a bit different."
msgstr "Pesan bantuannya sedikit berbeda."

msgid ""
"When using the ``--verbosity`` option, one must also specify some value, any "
"value."
msgstr ""
"Saat menggunakan opsi ``--verbosity``, kita juga harus menentukan suatu "
"nilai, nilai apa pun."

msgid ""
"The above example accepts arbitrary integer values for ``--verbosity``, but "
"for our simple program, only two values are actually useful, ``True`` or "
"``False``. Let's modify the code accordingly::"
msgstr ""
"Contoh di atas menerima nilai bilangan bulat apa pun untuk ``--verbosity``, "
"tetapi untuk program sederhana kita, hanya dua nilai yang benar-benar "
"berguna, ``True`` atau ``False``. Mari kita ubah kodenya::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"--verbose\", help=\"increase output verbosity\",\n"
"                    action=\"store_true\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"if args.verbose:\n"
"    print(\"verbosity turned on\")"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"--verbose\", help=\"increase output verbosity\",\n"
"                    action=\"store_true\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"if args.verbose:\n"
"    print(\"verbosity turned on\")"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py --verbose\n"
"verbosity turned on\n"
"$ python prog.py --verbose 1\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [--verbose]\n"
"prog.py: error: unrecognized arguments: 1\n"
"$ python prog.py --help\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [--verbose]\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help  show this help message and exit\n"
"  --verbose   increase output verbosity"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py --verbose\n"
"verbosity turned on\n"
"$ python prog.py --verbose 1\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [--verbose]\n"
"prog.py: error: unrecognized arguments: 1\n"
"$ python prog.py --help\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [--verbose]\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help  show this help message and exit\n"
"  --verbose   increase output verbosity"

msgid ""
"The option is now more of a flag than something that requires a value. We "
"even changed the name of the option to match that idea. Note that we now "
"specify a new keyword, ``action``, and give it the value ``\"store_true\"``. "
"This means that, if the option is specified, assign the value ``True`` to "
"``args.verbose``. Not specifying it implies ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Opsi ini sekarang lebih seperti sebuah flag daripada sesuatu yang "
"membutuhkan nilai. Kita bahkan mengubah nama opsi agar sesuai dengan ide "
"tersebut. Perlu diperhatikan bahwa kita sekarang menentukan kata kunci baru, "
"``action``, dan memberinya nilai ``\"store_true\"``. Artinya, jika opsi "
"ditentukan, berikan nilai ``True`` ke ``args.verbose``. Jika tidak "
"ditentukan, nilainya adalah ``False``."

msgid ""
"It complains when you specify a value, in true spirit of what flags actually "
"are."
msgstr ""
"Parser menolak argumen tersebut jika Anda menyertakan nilai, sesuai dengan "
"sifat sebuah flag."

msgid "Notice the different help text."
msgstr "Perhatikan teks bantuan yang berbeda."

msgid "Short options"
msgstr "Opsi pendek"

msgid ""
"If you are familiar with command line usage, you will notice that I haven't "
"yet touched on the topic of short versions of the options. It's quite "
"simple::"
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda sudah familier dengan penggunaan baris perintah, Anda akan melihat "
"bahwa saya belum menyentuh topik versi pendek dari opsi-opsi tersebut. "
"Caranya cukup sederhana::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbose\", help=\"increase output "
"verbosity\",\n"
"                    action=\"store_true\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"if args.verbose:\n"
"    print(\"verbosity turned on\")"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbose\", help=\"increase output "
"verbosity\",\n"
"                    action=\"store_true\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"if args.verbose:\n"
"    print(\"verbosity turned on\")"

msgid "And here goes:"
msgstr "Dan beginilah hasilnya:"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py -v\n"
"verbosity turned on\n"
"$ python prog.py --help\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v]\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help     show this help message and exit\n"
"  -v, --verbose  increase output verbosity"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py -v\n"
"verbosity turned on\n"
"$ python prog.py --help\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v]\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help     show this help message and exit\n"
"  -v, --verbose  increase output verbosity"

msgid "Note that the new ability is also reflected in the help text."
msgstr ""
"Perlu diperhatikan bahwa kemampuan baru ini juga tercermin dalam teks "
"bantuan."

msgid "Combining Positional and Optional arguments"
msgstr "Menggabungkan Argumen Posisional dan Opsional"

msgid "Our program keeps growing in complexity::"
msgstr "Program kita terus bertambah kompleks::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"display a square of a given number\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbose\", action=\"store_true\",\n"
"                    help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.square**2\n"
"if args.verbose:\n"
"    print(f\"the square of {args.square} equals {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"display a square of a given number\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbose\", action=\"store_true\",\n"
"                    help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.square**2\n"
"if args.verbose:\n"
"    print(f\"the square of {args.square} equals {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"

msgid "And now the output:"
msgstr "Dan sekarang keluarannya:"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v] square\n"
"prog.py: error: the following arguments are required: square\n"
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 --verbose\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py --verbose 4\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v] square\n"
"prog.py: error: the following arguments are required: square\n"
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 --verbose\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py --verbose 4\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16"

msgid "We've brought back a positional argument, hence the complaint."
msgstr ""
"Kita telah menambahkan kembali argumen posisional, sehingga muncul keluhan "
"tersebut."

msgid "Note that the order does not matter."
msgstr "Perlu diperhatikan bahwa urutannya tidak penting."

msgid ""
"How about we give this program of ours back the ability to have multiple "
"verbosity values, and actually get to use them::"
msgstr ""
"Bagaimana kalau kita mengembalikan kemampuan program kita untuk memiliki "
"beberapa nilai verbosity, dan benar-benar menggunakannya::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"display a square of a given number\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.square**2\n"
"if args.verbosity == 2:\n"
"    print(f\"the square of {args.square} equals {answer}\")\n"
"elif args.verbosity == 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.square}^2 == {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"display a square of a given number\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.square**2\n"
"if args.verbosity == 2:\n"
"    print(f\"the square of {args.square} equals {answer}\")\n"
"elif args.verbosity == 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.square}^2 == {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -v\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v VERBOSITY] square\n"
"prog.py: error: argument -v/--verbosity: expected one argument\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -v 1\n"
"4^2 == 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -v 2\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -v 3\n"
"16"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -v\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v VERBOSITY] square\n"
"prog.py: error: argument -v/--verbosity: expected one argument\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -v 1\n"
"4^2 == 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -v 2\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -v 3\n"
"16"

msgid ""
"These all look good except the last one, which exposes a bug in our program. "
"Let's fix it by restricting the values the ``--verbosity`` option can "
"accept::"
msgstr ""
"Semua ini terlihat bagus kecuali yang terakhir, yang mengungkapkan adanya "
"bug dalam program kita. Mari kita perbaiki dengan membatasi nilai yang dapat "
"diterima oleh opsi ``--verbosity``::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"display a square of a given number\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", type=int, choices=[0, 1, 2],\n"
"                    help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.square**2\n"
"if args.verbosity == 2:\n"
"    print(f\"the square of {args.square} equals {answer}\")\n"
"elif args.verbosity == 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.square}^2 == {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"display a square of a given number\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", type=int, choices=[0, 1, 2],\n"
"                    help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.square**2\n"
"if args.verbosity == 2:\n"
"    print(f\"the square of {args.square} equals {answer}\")\n"
"elif args.verbosity == 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.square}^2 == {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py 4 -v 3\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v {0,1,2}] square\n"
"prog.py: error: argument -v/--verbosity: invalid choice: 3 (choose from 0, "
"1, 2)\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -h\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v {0,1,2}] square\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  square                display a square of a given number\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n"
"  -v, --verbosity {0,1,2}\n"
"                        increase output verbosity"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py 4 -v 3\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v {0,1,2}] square\n"
"prog.py: error: argument -v/--verbosity: invalid choice: 3 (choose from 0, "
"1, 2)\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -h\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v {0,1,2}] square\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  square                display a square of a given number\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n"
"  -v, --verbosity {0,1,2}\n"
"                        increase output verbosity"

msgid ""
"Note that the change also reflects both in the error message as well as the "
"help string."
msgstr ""
"Perlu diperhatikan bahwa perubahan tersebut juga tercermin baik dalam pesan "
"galat maupun dalam string bantuan."

msgid ""
"Now, let's use a different approach of playing with verbosity, which is "
"pretty common. It also matches the way the CPython executable handles its "
"own verbosity argument (check the output of ``python --help``)::"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, mari kita gunakan pendekatan berbeda dalam bermain-main dengan "
"verbosity, yang cukup umum. Pendekatan ini juga cocok dengan cara executable "
"CPython menangani argumen verbosity-nya sendiri (periksa keluaran dari "
"``python --help``)::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"display the square of a given number\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", action=\"count\",\n"
"                    help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.square**2\n"
"if args.verbosity == 2:\n"
"    print(f\"the square of {args.square} equals {answer}\")\n"
"elif args.verbosity == 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.square}^2 == {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"display the square of a given number\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", action=\"count\",\n"
"                    help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.square**2\n"
"if args.verbosity == 2:\n"
"    print(f\"the square of {args.square} equals {answer}\")\n"
"elif args.verbosity == 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.square}^2 == {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"

msgid ""
"We have introduced another action, \"count\", to count the number of "
"occurrences of specific options."
msgstr ""
"Kita telah memperkenalkan aksi lain, \"count\", untuk menghitung jumlah "
"kemunculan opsi tertentu."

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -v\n"
"4^2 == 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -vv\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 --verbosity --verbosity\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -v 1\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v] square\n"
"prog.py: error: unrecognized arguments: 1\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -h\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v] square\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  square           display a square of a given number\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help       show this help message and exit\n"
"  -v, --verbosity  increase output verbosity\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -vvv\n"
"16"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -v\n"
"4^2 == 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -vv\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 --verbosity --verbosity\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -v 1\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v] square\n"
"prog.py: error: unrecognized arguments: 1\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -h\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v] square\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  square           display a square of a given number\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help       show this help message and exit\n"
"  -v, --verbosity  increase output verbosity\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -vvv\n"
"16"

msgid ""
"Yes, it's now more of a flag (similar to ``action=\"store_true\"``) in the "
"previous version of our script. That should explain the complaint."
msgstr ""
"Ya, opsi ini sekarang lebih seperti sebuah flag (mirip dengan "
"``action=\"store_true\"``) pada versi skrip kita sebelumnya. Itu seharusnya "
"menjelaskan keluhan tersebut."

msgid "It also behaves similar to \"store_true\" action."
msgstr "Opsi ini juga berperilaku mirip dengan aksi \"store_true\"."

msgid ""
"Now here's a demonstration of what the \"count\" action gives. You've "
"probably seen this sort of usage before."
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, berikut adalah demonstrasi dari apa yang diberikan oleh aksi "
"\"count\". Anda mungkin pernah melihat penggunaan semacam ini sebelumnya."

msgid ""
"And if you don't specify the ``-v`` flag, that flag is considered to have "
"``None`` value."
msgstr ""
"Dan jika Anda tidak menentukan flag ``-v``, flag tersebut dianggap memiliki "
"nilai ``None``."

msgid ""
"As should be expected, specifying the long form of the flag, we should get "
"the same output."
msgstr ""
"Sebagaimana mestinya, jika kita menentukan bentuk panjang dari flag "
"tersebut, kita seharusnya mendapatkan keluaran yang sama."

msgid ""
"Sadly, our help output isn't very informative on the new ability our script "
"has acquired, but that can always be fixed by improving the documentation "
"for our script (e.g. via the ``help`` keyword argument)."
msgstr ""
"Sayangnya, keluaran bantuan kita tidak terlalu informatif tentang kemampuan "
"baru yang diperoleh skrip kita, tetapi hal itu selalu dapat diperbaiki "
"dengan meningkatkan dokumentasi untuk skrip kita (misalnya melalui argumen "
"kata kunci ``help``)."

msgid "That last output exposes a bug in our program."
msgstr ""
"Keluaran terakhir tersebut mengungkapkan adanya bug dalam program kita."

msgid "Let's fix::"
msgstr "Mari kita perbaiki::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"display a square of a given number\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", action=\"count\",\n"
"                    help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.square**2\n"
"\n"
"# bugfix: replace == with >=\n"
"if args.verbosity >= 2:\n"
"    print(f\"the square of {args.square} equals {answer}\")\n"
"elif args.verbosity >= 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.square}^2 == {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"display a square of a given number\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", action=\"count\",\n"
"                    help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.square**2\n"
"\n"
"# bugfix: replace == with >=\n"
"if args.verbosity >= 2:\n"
"    print(f\"the square of {args.square} equals {answer}\")\n"
"elif args.verbosity >= 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.square}^2 == {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"

msgid "And this is what it gives:"
msgstr "Dan inilah hasilnya:"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py 4 -vvv\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -vvvv\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"  File \"prog.py\", line 11, in <module>\n"
"    if args.verbosity >= 2:\n"
"TypeError: '>=' not supported between instances of 'NoneType' and 'int'"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py 4 -vvv\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 -vvvv\n"
"the square of 4 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"  File \"prog.py\", line 11, in <module>\n"
"    if args.verbosity >= 2:\n"
"TypeError: '>=' not supported between instances of 'NoneType' and 'int'"

msgid ""
"First output went well, and fixes the bug we had before. That is, we want "
"any value >= 2 to be as verbose as possible."
msgstr ""
"Keluaran pertama berjalan dengan baik, dan memperbaiki bug yang kita miliki "
"sebelumnya. Artinya, kita menginginkan nilai apa pun yang >= 2 menjadi "
"verbose secara maksimal."

msgid "Third output not so good."
msgstr "Keluaran ketiga tidak begitu bagus."

msgid "Let's fix that bug::"
msgstr "Mari kita perbaiki bug tersebut::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"display a square of a given number\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", action=\"count\", default=0,\n"
"                    help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.square**2\n"
"if args.verbosity >= 2:\n"
"    print(f\"the square of {args.square} equals {answer}\")\n"
"elif args.verbosity >= 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.square}^2 == {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"square\", type=int,\n"
"                    help=\"display a square of a given number\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", action=\"count\", default=0,\n"
"                    help=\"increase output verbosity\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.square**2\n"
"if args.verbosity >= 2:\n"
"    print(f\"the square of {args.square} equals {answer}\")\n"
"elif args.verbosity >= 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.square}^2 == {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"

msgid ""
"We've just introduced yet another keyword, ``default``. We've set it to "
"``0`` in order to make it comparable to the other int values. Remember that "
"by default, if an optional argument isn't specified, it gets the ``None`` "
"value, and that cannot be compared to an int value (hence "
"the :exc:`TypeError` exception)."
msgstr ""
"Kita baru saja memperkenalkan kata kunci lain, ``default``. Kita mengaturnya "
"ke ``0`` agar dapat dibandingkan dengan nilai int lainnya. Ingatlah bahwa "
"secara default, jika argumen opsional tidak ditentukan, nilainya adalah "
"``None``, dan nilai tersebut tidak dapat dibandingkan dengan nilai int "
"(sehingga muncul eksepsi :exc:`TypeError`)."

msgid "And:"
msgstr "Dan:"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"16"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py 4\n"
"16"

msgid ""
"You can go quite far just with what we've learned so far, and we have only "
"scratched the surface. The :mod:`argparse` module is very powerful, and "
"we'll explore a bit more of it before we end this tutorial."
msgstr ""
"Anda bisa melangkah cukup jauh hanya dengan apa yang telah kita pelajari "
"sejauh ini, dan kita baru saja menyentuh permukaannya. Modul :mod:`argparse` "
"sangat kuat, dan kita akan menjelajahi sedikit lebih banyak lagi sebelum "
"kita mengakhiri tutorial ini."

msgid "Getting a little more advanced"
msgstr "Melangkah sedikit lebih jauh"

msgid ""
"What if we wanted to expand our tiny program to perform other powers, not "
"just squares::"
msgstr ""
"Bagaimana jika kita ingin memperluas program kecil kita untuk melakukan "
"perpangkatan lain, bukan hanya kuadrat::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"x\", type=int, help=\"the base\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"y\", type=int, help=\"the exponent\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", action=\"count\", default=0)\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.x**args.y\n"
"if args.verbosity >= 2:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x} to the power {args.y} equals {answer}\")\n"
"elif args.verbosity >= 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x}^{args.y} == {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"x\", type=int, help=\"the base\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"y\", type=int, help=\"the exponent\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", action=\"count\", default=0)\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.x**args.y\n"
"if args.verbosity >= 2:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x} to the power {args.y} equals {answer}\")\n"
"elif args.verbosity >= 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x}^{args.y} == {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(answer)"

msgid "Output:"
msgstr "Keluaran:"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v] x y\n"
"prog.py: error: the following arguments are required: x, y\n"
"$ python prog.py -h\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v] x y\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  x                the base\n"
"  y                the exponent\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help       show this help message and exit\n"
"  -v, --verbosity\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -v\n"
"4^2 == 16"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v] x y\n"
"prog.py: error: the following arguments are required: x, y\n"
"$ python prog.py -h\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v] x y\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  x                the base\n"
"  y                the exponent\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help       show this help message and exit\n"
"  -v, --verbosity\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -v\n"
"4^2 == 16"

msgid ""
"Notice that so far we've been using verbosity level to *change* the text "
"that gets displayed. The following example instead uses verbosity level to "
"display *more* text instead::"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa sejauh ini kita telah menggunakan tingkat verbosity untuk "
"*mengubah* teks yang ditampilkan. Contoh berikut justru menggunakan tingkat "
"verbosity untuk menampilkan *lebih banyak* teks::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"x\", type=int, help=\"the base\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"y\", type=int, help=\"the exponent\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", action=\"count\", default=0)\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.x**args.y\n"
"if args.verbosity >= 2:\n"
"    print(f\"Running '{__file__}'\")\n"
"if args.verbosity >= 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x}^{args.y} == \", end=\"\")\n"
"print(answer)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"x\", type=int, help=\"the base\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"y\", type=int, help=\"the exponent\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbosity\", action=\"count\", default=0)\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.x**args.y\n"
"if args.verbosity >= 2:\n"
"    print(f\"Running '{__file__}'\")\n"
"if args.verbosity >= 1:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x}^{args.y} == \", end=\"\")\n"
"print(answer)"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py 4 2\n"
"16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -v\n"
"4^2 == 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -vv\n"
"Running 'prog.py'\n"
"4^2 == 16"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py 4 2\n"
"16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -v\n"
"4^2 == 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -vv\n"
"Running 'prog.py'\n"
"4^2 == 16"

msgid "Specifying ambiguous arguments"
msgstr "Menentukan argumen yang ambigu"

msgid ""
"When there is ambiguity in deciding whether an argument is positional or for "
"an argument, ``--`` can be used to tell :meth:`~ArgumentParser.parse_args` "
"that everything after that is a positional argument::"
msgstr ""
"Ketika ada ambiguitas dalam menentukan apakah sebuah argumen bersifat "
"posisional atau merupakan argumen untuk sebuah opsi, ``--`` dapat digunakan "
"untuk memberi tahu :meth:`~ArgumentParser.parse_args` bahwa semua yang ada "
"setelah itu adalah argumen posisional::"

msgid ""
">>> parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog='PROG')\n"
">>> parser.add_argument('-n', nargs='+')\n"
">>> parser.add_argument('args', nargs='*')\n"
"\n"
">>> # ambiguous, so parse_args assumes it's an option\n"
">>> parser.parse_args(['-f'])\n"
"usage: PROG [-h] [-n N [N ...]] [args ...]\n"
"PROG: error: unrecognized arguments: -f\n"
"\n"
">>> parser.parse_args(['--', '-f'])\n"
"Namespace(args=['-f'], n=None)\n"
"\n"
">>> # ambiguous, so the -n option greedily accepts arguments\n"
">>> parser.parse_args(['-n', '1', '2', '3'])\n"
"Namespace(args=[], n=['1', '2', '3'])\n"
"\n"
">>> parser.parse_args(['-n', '1', '--', '2', '3'])\n"
"Namespace(args=['2', '3'], n=['1'])"
msgstr ""
">>> parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog='PROG')\n"
">>> parser.add_argument('-n', nargs='+')\n"
">>> parser.add_argument('args', nargs='*')\n"
"\n"
">>> # ambiguous, so parse_args assumes it's an option\n"
">>> parser.parse_args(['-f'])\n"
"usage: PROG [-h] [-n N [N ...]] [args ...]\n"
"PROG: error: unrecognized arguments: -f\n"
"\n"
">>> parser.parse_args(['--', '-f'])\n"
"Namespace(args=['-f'], n=None)\n"
"\n"
">>> # ambiguous, so the -n option greedily accepts arguments\n"
">>> parser.parse_args(['-n', '1', '2', '3'])\n"
"Namespace(args=[], n=['1', '2', '3'])\n"
"\n"
">>> parser.parse_args(['-n', '1', '--', '2', '3'])\n"
"Namespace(args=['2', '3'], n=['1'])"

msgid "Conflicting options"
msgstr "Opsi yang saling bertentangan"

msgid ""
"So far, we have been working with two methods of "
"an :class:`argparse.ArgumentParser` instance. Let's introduce a third "
"one, :meth:`~ArgumentParser.add_mutually_exclusive_group`. It allows for us "
"to specify options that conflict with each other. Let's also change the rest "
"of the program so that the new functionality makes more sense: we'll "
"introduce the ``--quiet`` option, which will be the opposite of the ``--"
"verbose`` one::"
msgstr ""
"Sejauh ini, kita telah bekerja dengan dua metode dari sebuah "
"instance :class:`argparse.ArgumentParser`. Mari kita perkenalkan metode "
"ketiga, :meth:`~ArgumentParser.add_mutually_exclusive_group`. Metode ini "
"memungkinkan kita menentukan opsi-opsi yang saling bertentangan. Mari kita "
"ubah juga sisa program agar fungsionalitas baru ini lebih masuk akal: kita "
"akan memperkenalkan opsi ``--quiet``, yang akan menjadi kebalikan dari opsi "
"``--verbose``::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"group = parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group()\n"
"group.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbose\", action=\"store_true\")\n"
"group.add_argument(\"-q\", \"--quiet\", action=\"store_true\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"x\", type=int, help=\"the base\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"y\", type=int, help=\"the exponent\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.x**args.y\n"
"\n"
"if args.quiet:\n"
"    print(answer)\n"
"elif args.verbose:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x} to the power {args.y} equals {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x}^{args.y} == {answer}\")"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n"
"group = parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group()\n"
"group.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbose\", action=\"store_true\")\n"
"group.add_argument(\"-q\", \"--quiet\", action=\"store_true\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"x\", type=int, help=\"the base\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"y\", type=int, help=\"the exponent\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.x**args.y\n"
"\n"
"if args.quiet:\n"
"    print(answer)\n"
"elif args.verbose:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x} to the power {args.y} equals {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x}^{args.y} == {answer}\")"

msgid ""
"Our program is now simpler, and we've lost some functionality for the sake "
"of demonstration. Anyways, here's the output:"
msgstr ""
"Program kita sekarang lebih sederhana, dan kita telah kehilangan sebagian "
"fungsionalitas demi demonstrasi. Bagaimanapun, inilah keluarannya:"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py 4 2\n"
"4^2 == 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -q\n"
"16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -v\n"
"4 to the power 2 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -vq\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v | -q] x y\n"
"prog.py: error: argument -q/--quiet: not allowed with argument -v/--verbose\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -v --quiet\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v | -q] x y\n"
"prog.py: error: argument -q/--quiet: not allowed with argument -v/--verbose"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py 4 2\n"
"4^2 == 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -q\n"
"16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -v\n"
"4 to the power 2 equals 16\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -vq\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v | -q] x y\n"
"prog.py: error: argument -q/--quiet: not allowed with argument -v/--verbose\n"
"$ python prog.py 4 2 -v --quiet\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v | -q] x y\n"
"prog.py: error: argument -q/--quiet: not allowed with argument -v/--verbose"

msgid ""
"That should be easy to follow. I've added that last output so you can see "
"the sort of flexibility you get, i.e. mixing long form options with short "
"form ones."
msgstr ""
"Itu seharusnya mudah diikuti. Saya menambahkan keluaran terakhir itu agar "
"Anda dapat melihat fleksibilitas yang Anda dapatkan, yaitu mencampur opsi "
"bentuk panjang dengan opsi bentuk pendek."

msgid ""
"Before we conclude, you probably want to tell your users the main purpose of "
"your program, just in case they don't know::"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum kita mengakhiri, Anda mungkin ingin memberi tahu pengguna Anda "
"tujuan utama program Anda, untuk berjaga-jaga jika mereka tidak "
"mengetahuinya::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"calculate X to the power of "
"Y\")\n"
"group = parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group()\n"
"group.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbose\", action=\"store_true\")\n"
"group.add_argument(\"-q\", \"--quiet\", action=\"store_true\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"x\", type=int, help=\"the base\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"y\", type=int, help=\"the exponent\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.x**args.y\n"
"\n"
"if args.quiet:\n"
"    print(answer)\n"
"elif args.verbose:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x} to the power {args.y} equals {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x}^{args.y} == {answer}\")"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"calculate X to the power of "
"Y\")\n"
"group = parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group()\n"
"group.add_argument(\"-v\", \"--verbose\", action=\"store_true\")\n"
"group.add_argument(\"-q\", \"--quiet\", action=\"store_true\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"x\", type=int, help=\"the base\")\n"
"parser.add_argument(\"y\", type=int, help=\"the exponent\")\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"answer = args.x**args.y\n"
"\n"
"if args.quiet:\n"
"    print(answer)\n"
"elif args.verbose:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x} to the power {args.y} equals {answer}\")\n"
"else:\n"
"    print(f\"{args.x}^{args.y} == {answer}\")"

msgid ""
"Note that slight difference in the usage text. Note the ``[-v | -q]``, which "
"tells us that we can either use ``-v`` or ``-q``, but not both at the same "
"time:"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan sedikit perbedaan dalam teks penggunaan. Perhatikan ``[-v | "
"-q]``, yang memberi tahu kita bahwa kita dapat menggunakan ``-v`` atau "
"``-q``, tetapi tidak keduanya pada saat yang bersamaan:"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py --help\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v | -q] x y\n"
"\n"
"calculate X to the power of Y\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  x              the base\n"
"  y              the exponent\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help     show this help message and exit\n"
"  -v, --verbose\n"
"  -q, --quiet"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py --help\n"
"usage: prog.py [-h] [-v | -q] x y\n"
"\n"
"calculate X to the power of Y\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  x              the base\n"
"  y              the exponent\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help     show this help message and exit\n"
"  -v, --verbose\n"
"  -q, --quiet"

msgid "How to translate the argparse output"
msgstr "Cara menerjemahkan keluaran argparse"

msgid ""
"The output of the :mod:`argparse` module such as its help text and error "
"messages are all made translatable using the :mod:`gettext` module. This "
"allows applications to easily localize messages produced by :mod:`argparse`. "
"See also :ref:`i18n-howto`."
msgstr ""
"Keluaran dari modul :mod:`argparse`, seperti teks bantuan dan pesan "
"galatnya, semuanya dibuat dapat diterjemahkan menggunakan "
"modul :mod:`gettext`. Hal ini memungkinkan aplikasi dengan mudah melokalkan "
"pesan yang dihasilkan oleh :mod:`argparse`. Lihat juga :ref:`i18n-howto`."

msgid "For instance, in this :mod:`argparse` output:"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh, dalam keluaran :mod:`argparse` ini:"

msgid ""
"The strings ``usage:``, ``positional arguments:``, ``options:`` and ``show "
"this help message and exit`` are all translatable."
msgstr ""
"String ``usage:``, ``positional arguments:``, ``options:``, dan ``show this "
"help message and exit`` semuanya dapat diterjemahkan."

msgid ""
"In order to translate these strings, they must first be extracted into a "
"``.po`` file. For example, using `Babel <https://babel.pocoo.org/>`__, run "
"this command:"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menerjemahkan string-string ini, semuanya harus terlebih dahulu "
"diekstrak ke dalam berkas ``.po``. Sebagai contoh, dengan menggunakan `Babel "
"<https://babel.pocoo.org/>`__, jalankan perintah ini:"

msgid "$ pybabel extract -o messages.po /usr/lib/python3.12/argparse.py"
msgstr "$ pybabel extract -o messages.po /usr/lib/python3.12/argparse.py"

msgid ""
"This command will extract all translatable strings from the :mod:`argparse` "
"module and output them into a file named ``messages.po``. This command "
"assumes that your Python installation is in ``/usr/lib``."
msgstr ""
"Perintah ini akan mengekstrak semua string yang dapat diterjemahkan dari "
"modul :mod:`argparse` dan mengeluarkannya ke dalam berkas bernama "
"``messages.po``. Perintah ini mengasumsikan bahwa instalasi Python Anda "
"berada di ``/usr/lib``."

msgid ""
"You can find out the location of the :mod:`argparse` module on your system "
"using this script::"
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat mengetahui lokasi modul :mod:`argparse` di sistem Anda "
"menggunakan skrip ini::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"print(argparse.__file__)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"print(argparse.__file__)"

msgid ""
"Once the messages in the ``.po`` file are translated and the translations "
"are installed using :mod:`gettext`, :mod:`argparse` will be able to display "
"the translated messages."
msgstr ""
"Setelah pesan-pesan dalam berkas ``.po`` diterjemahkan dan terjemahannya "
"dipasang menggunakan :mod:`gettext`, :mod:`argparse` akan dapat menampilkan "
"pesan yang telah diterjemahkan."

msgid ""
"To translate your own strings in the :mod:`argparse` output, "
"use :mod:`gettext`."
msgstr ""
"Untuk menerjemahkan string Anda sendiri dalam keluaran :mod:`argparse`, "
"gunakan :mod:`gettext`."

msgid "Custom type converters"
msgstr "Konverter tipe kustom"

msgid ""
"The :mod:`argparse` module allows you to specify custom type converters for "
"your command-line arguments. This allows you to modify user input before "
"it's stored in the :class:`argparse.Namespace`. This can be useful when you "
"need to pre-process the input before it is used in your program."
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`argparse` memungkinkan Anda menentukan konverter tipe kustom "
"untuk argumen baris perintah Anda. Hal ini memungkinkan Anda memodifikasi "
"input pengguna sebelum disimpan dalam :class:`argparse.Namespace`. Ini bisa "
"berguna saat Anda perlu memproses input terlebih dahulu sebelum digunakan "
"dalam program Anda."

msgid ""
"When using a custom type converter, you can use any callable that takes a "
"single string argument (the argument value) and returns the converted value. "
"However, if you need to handle more complex scenarios, you can use a custom "
"action class with the **action** parameter instead."
msgstr ""
"Saat menggunakan konverter tipe kustom, Anda dapat menggunakan callable apa "
"pun yang menerima satu argumen string (nilai argumen) dan mengembalikan "
"nilai yang telah dikonversi. Namun, jika Anda perlu menangani skenario yang "
"lebih kompleks, Anda dapat menggunakan kelas aksi kustom dengan parameter "
"**action** sebagai gantinya."

msgid ""
"For example, let's say you want to handle arguments with different prefixes "
"and process them accordingly::"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, katakanlah Anda ingin menangani argumen dengan prefiks yang "
"berbeda dan memprosesnya sesuai dengan prefiks tersebut::"

msgid ""
"import argparse\n"
"\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prefix_chars='-+')\n"
"\n"
"parser.add_argument('-a', metavar='<value>', action='append',\n"
"                    type=lambda x: ('-', x))\n"
"parser.add_argument('+a', metavar='<value>', action='append',\n"
"                    type=lambda x: ('+', x))\n"
"\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"print(args)"
msgstr ""
"import argparse\n"
"\n"
"parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prefix_chars='-+')\n"
"\n"
"parser.add_argument('-a', metavar='<value>', action='append',\n"
"                    type=lambda x: ('-', x))\n"
"parser.add_argument('+a', metavar='<value>', action='append',\n"
"                    type=lambda x: ('+', x))\n"
"\n"
"args = parser.parse_args()\n"
"print(args)"

msgid ""
"$ python prog.py -a value1 +a value2\n"
"Namespace(a=[('-', 'value1'), ('+', 'value2')])"
msgstr ""
"$ python prog.py -a value1 +a value2\n"
"Namespace(a=[('-', 'value1'), ('+', 'value2')])"

msgid "In this example, we:"
msgstr "Dalam contoh ini, kita:"

msgid ""
"Created a parser with custom prefix characters using the ``prefix_chars`` "
"parameter."
msgstr ""
"Membuat parser dengan karakter prefiks kustom menggunakan parameter "
"``prefix_chars``."

msgid ""
"Defined two arguments, ``-a`` and ``+a``, which used the ``type`` parameter "
"to create custom type converters to store the value in a tuple with the "
"prefix."
msgstr ""
"Mendefinisikan dua argumen, ``-a`` dan ``+a``, yang menggunakan parameter "
"``type`` untuk membuat konverter tipe kustom guna menyimpan nilai dalam "
"sebuah tuple beserta prefiksnya."

msgid ""
"Without the custom type converters, the arguments would have treated the ``-"
"a`` and ``+a`` as the same argument, which would have been undesirable. By "
"using custom type converters, we were able to differentiate between the two "
"arguments."
msgstr ""
"Tanpa konverter tipe kustom, argumen-argumen tersebut akan memperlakukan "
"``-a`` dan ``+a`` sebagai argumen yang sama, yang tentunya tidak diinginkan. "
"Dengan menggunakan konverter tipe kustom, kita dapat membedakan kedua "
"argumen tersebut."

msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr "Kesimpulan"

msgid ""
"The :mod:`argparse` module offers a lot more than shown here. Its docs are "
"quite detailed and thorough, and full of examples. Having gone through this "
"tutorial, you should easily digest them without feeling overwhelmed."
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`argparse` menawarkan lebih banyak hal daripada yang ditunjukkan "
"di sini. Dokumentasinya cukup terperinci dan menyeluruh, serta penuh dengan "
"contoh. Setelah melalui tutorial ini, Anda seharusnya dapat dengan mudah "
"mencernanya tanpa merasa kewalahan."
